We investigate the impact of $b 	o c$ transition data on the decay of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ within the $U_1$ leptoquark model. By analyzing the $b 	o c$ transition, we determine the leptoquark's mass and coupling parameters, which in turn allow us to predict the branching ratio of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ and the associated angular distribution. Our findings indicate that the $b 	o c$ transition data significantly constrain the leptoquark's mass and coupling parameters, which in turn affect the predicted branching ratio and angular distribution of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$.
